{title:Rest In Peace}
{key:}

When there's no room to manoeuvre through the cracks in your soul
No more demons left to target with your imaginary darts
Will the resentment that you painted onto the skin of your own torment
Create a parasol of confusion that casts shadows on your heart

When all time and all space is devoid of all meaning
Will the sound of your own voice be like fresh snow to the touch
Will owning your very own instruments of torture
Be like knowing that what you know, doesn't count for very much

When all is said and done and all corners have been vacated
Will the writing on the wall turn to jumbled letters on the floor
When all races have been run and all disappointments have been tasted
Will there be fog on the mirror of your life any more

Will you find peace at last?
Yes indeed you will find peace at last
You will rise and in objective glory you will go
I will watch your ascent into the eternity
That you will never know